{"availability":"available","full":"Liu-Tianchi/EmoTra-TTS","name":"EmoTra-TTS","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":62,"forks":8,"created":"2026-08-10T16:59:36Z","updated":"2026-08-26T10:31:36Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://liu-tianchi.github.io/EmoTra_DemoPage/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:28.321Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:28.321Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:58:28.321Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.575Z","stars":175,"forks":8},{"at":"2026-10-17T02:58:28.321Z","stars":62,"forks":8}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Official code release for the EMNLP 2026 paper","“EmoTra-TTS: Smooth Intra-Utterance Emotion Transitions for Speech Synthesis”","EmoTra-TTS is a two-stage fine-tuning framework built on CosyVoice 2 that enables continuous emotion control in speech synthesis using Valence–Arousal–Dominance (VAD) representations. Instead of discrete emotion labels, it takes 3D VAD vectors for the start and end emotional states and synthesizes speech that transitions smoothly between them — all within a single utterance."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Liu-Tianchi/EmoTra-TTS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0f902299bba1df7be429d10f5fed6c3287f38f33e5abe53d316a906c5789d7e7","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.782Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.782Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Official code release for the EMNLP 2026 paper","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Liu-Tianchi/EmoTra-TTS/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0f902299bba1df7be429d10f5fed6c3287f38f33e5abe53d316a906c5789d7e7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Liu-Tianchi/EmoTra-TTS/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:51.783Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-26T10:31:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status